==Spanish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{es-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|la|es}} {{m|la|vae||woe}} or {{etyl|got|es}} {{m|got|𐍅𐌰𐌹||woe}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|es}} {{m|gem-pro|*wai}}, both from {{etyl|ine-pro|es}} {{m|ine-pro|*wai}}. Cognate with {{cog|pt|guai}} and {{cog|it|guai}}.

====Interjection====
{{es-interj}}

# {{lb|es|obsolete}} {{l|en|woe}}! {{gloss|expresses grief}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|es|ay}}

===Etymology 2===
{{unk|es}}, maybe related to French {{m|fr|gai}}, Italian {{m|it|gaio}}, English {{m|en|gay}} of Germanic origin or from Arabic {{m|ar|كويس||tr=kuwayyis}}.

====Adjective====
{{es-adj|pl=guay|pl2=guais}}

# {{lb|es|Spain|slang}} [[cool]]

=====Usage notes=====
* This adjective is most often treated as invariable, with the form {{m|es||guay}} being used regardless of gender or number; however, the plural form {{m|es|guais}} is also often found. Hence, “They're very cool” may be expressed either as ''son muy guay'' or as ''son muy guais''.

====Adverb====
{{es-adv}}

# {{lb|es|Spain|slang}} [[cool]]

=====Usage notes=====
* Often expanded to '''guay de Paraguay'''.

